<hr><h2 id="section-5">Shared Districts with Candidate Filing Office in Another County</h2><p>Some voting districts are "shared" and have voters in more than one county. Candidates <strong>only </strong>file their candidacy with their position's designated filing officer (county where the district's administrative office is located; city elections official; Dept. of Agriculture, Oregon Secretary of State). After the filing period ends, filing officers certify the list of filed candidates to the county elections officials in counties that have district voters. &nbsp;</p><p>Visit neighboring elections offices' websites to view information and filings for the shared districts managed by those counties:&nbsp;</p><ul><li><span>Filing Office: </span><a href="https://www.columbiacountyor.gov/departments/Elections" data-entity-type="external">Columbia <span>County</span></a><span>: Columbia River People's Utility District, subdivision 1</span></li></ul></div>
      
          </div>
  
      
  
